==== the live multiplayer route, chrome, against the public URL
checker : /Users/user/data/src/armagetronad-web/.worktrees/m5-launch/docs/evidence/m5-launch/check-live-multiplayer.mjs
source  : /Users/user/data/src/armagetronad-web/.worktrees/m5-launch/docs/evidence/m5-launch/live-mp-chrome/console.log

ok   baseline: the unmutated input passes (exit 0, 12 checks, 0 failures)

ok   X1a the run was against the local rig, not the deployment
       expected FAIL: X1   observed: X1   exit 1
       this is precisely what task 3 could NOT rule out about its own numbers, and it is why X1 exists: every figure in that task came from https://localhost:8443 behind a self-signed certificate.
ok   X1b the page reported itself as http:
       expected FAIL: X1   observed: X1   exit 1
       the second conjunct, and the independent one: the driver says what it was TOLD to open, the page says what it actually IS.
ok   X2  a consistent 19-attempt world, i.e. the http: figure
       expected FAIL: X2   observed: X2   exit 1
       mutated CONSISTENTLY -- summary, running total and browser lines all moved to 19 -- so X3 and X6 still agree with each other and only the band check fires. A lazier mutation of the one number would have knocked out three checks and proven none of them.
ok   X3  the browser recorded five fewer events than the module made attempts
       expected FAIL: X3   observed: X3   exit 1
ok   X4a one attempt went somewhere that is not a master server
       expected FAIL: X4   observed: X4   exit 1
ok   X4b the page saw three distinct endpoints, not four
       expected FAIL: X4   observed: X4   exit 1
       the other conjunct: the per-URL map and the distinct count are two different in-page derivations and X4 asserts both.
ok   X5  the attempts spanned 40 s, not the 4x5 s master timeout
       expected FAIL: X5   observed: X5   exit 1
ok   X6a five sockets were opened before the master query was ever started
       expected FAIL: X6   observed: X6   exit 1
       if the page opened ws:// sockets on its own the count would not be attributable to the menu route at all.
ok   X6b seven more sockets were opened after the query finished
       expected FAIL: X6   observed: X6   exit 1
       the other conjunct, and the one that matters for the decision task 3 took: the noise is acceptable BECAUSE it is bounded and stops.
ok   X7  the GL context came back with an error after the master query
       expected FAIL: X7   observed: X7   exit 1
ok   X8a a THIRD exception text appears
       expected FAIL: X8   observed: X8   exit 1
       this is the case that shows the rule was not loosened. Firefox logs 192-194 [EXCEPTION] lines on this route and every gate in this project forbids the tag; X8 permits two texts by name and nothing else.
ok   X8b a PERMITTED text on a line that names no ws:// endpoint
       expected FAIL: X8   observed: X8   exit 1
       the second conjunct of the allowance. "was interrupted while the page was loading" is an ordinary Firefox message about any request; it is waved through only when the line is about a ws:// endpoint.
ok   X8c an ordinary hazard text appears in the run
       expected FAIL: X8   observed: X8   exit 1
ok   X9  Chrome stops naming mixed content, keeping the rest of the sentence
       expected FAIL: X9   observed: X9   exit 1
       the same substring separation seen from the other side: the per-attempt clause X3 counts is untouched, so X3 still passes and only X9 fires.
ok   X10 a wait expired instead of being satisfied
       expected FAIL: X10   observed: X10   exit 1
ok   X11 something other than the favicon 404s
       expected FAIL: X11   observed: X11   exit 1
ok   REAL CONTROL (not a mutation): task 3's Chrome run against the LOCAL RIG, not the deployment
       /Users/user/data/src/armagetronad-web/.worktrees/m5-launch/docs/evidence/m5-https/mp-https/console.log
       expected FAIL: X1   observed: X1   exit 1

